--- body ---
## Context
Child of tracker 1309. Adds `runtime.py notify --title --body` (desktop
`notify-send` where present, plus an alert file under the git common dir, rate
limited per condition, the pattern of the arena's `scripts/arena-watchdog.py`)
and decides on an out-of-session raid supervisor: a systemd user timer that runs
`raid-sitrep.py` and calls `notify` when the queue is not empty and no SITREP has
been written for 30 minutes (coordinator presumed dead). `notify` is also the
documented fallback whenever `can wake` answers no.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `notify` verb with a rate limit and a test (stubbed notify-send, alert file written)
- [ ] Decision recorded: build the supervisor or drop it, with raid-log evidence
      (as of 2026-10-28, 8 raids and no dead coordinator)
- [ ] If built: unit + timer installed by `bin/idh install`, documented in raid § Sitrep cadence
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-28, opus seat)
**Path.** `scripts/runtime_notify.py` (verb module per 1311's layout):
`notify --key K --title T --body B [--repeat 3600]`.
- Runs `notify-send -a idh` and writes an alert file plus a state file under
  `<git-common-dir>/idh-alerts/`, under flock as in forge.py `_update_cache`.
- A repeat within the window prints `SUPPRESSED K` and exits 0.
- Without notify-send it writes the alert file only and says so.

**Supervisor: defer, do not build here** (exit criterion 2: decision recorded). The blind-spot pass notes survivorship bias: a dead coordinator writes nothing, so the log cannot show one. Record the check that would settle it: count raids whose last line is not `QUEUE n=0` / a final SITREP, cross-checked with their sessions' end. Until that check runs, the supervisor stays a candidate, not a rejection. The raid log holds
11 RAID_START, 41 SITREP and 4 BREAKER lines and no dead coordinator; record
this with the counts. Fallback prose in sitrep.md: `can wake.*` answers 1, so
use `notify`.

**Refuse:** a systemd unit; `bin/idh install` changes.

**First failing test:**
`tests/test_runtime_notify.py::test_second_call_within_repeat_does_not_call_notify_send`.
Assert the stub's log has exactly 1 line after 2 calls; an alert-file-only
assertion passes with no stub on PATH. The real desktop popup is the author's
check.

**Feasibility:** PASS. sitrep.md is shared with 1311, which lands first (different wave).
